WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.160
Good morning, Hank. It's Tuesday, October 10th, 2017, and I'm sitting on a hotel floor in New York City,

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:08.220
which can only mean one thing: my new book,
Turtles All the Way Down is out now,

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.180
at least in the US, the UK, Ireland, Australia,
New Zealand, and several other countries.

00:00:12.180 --> 00:00:15.700
First things first, if you've already read the book,
thank you! I hope that you liked it.

00:00:15.700 --> 00:00:18.060
Also, please do not spoil it for other people.

00:00:18.060 --> 00:00:22.160
Okay, so I've created a spoiler-riffic subreddit— [DING!]
Hold on, that's the elevator.

00:00:22.160 --> 00:00:23.940
Oh man, it's 'me's all the way down.

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:25.900
I can't decide if I should wear a suit.

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.980
Oh, look who I picked up, it's a Hank!
—Hello.

00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:32.360
—Right, but to return to the topic at hand, I have created a spoiler-riffic subreddit for Turtles All the Way Down,

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.880
where people who have read the book can go and discuss it with each other,

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:36.900
and also ask questions of me directly.

00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:39.280
There's a link in the doobly-doo below.
We have to go to our rehearsal now.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:44.340
We're about to go on stage before our rehearsal show,
and I'm super stressed out, and Hank's just, like, chilling.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.920
—I'm looking up how many people in the United States are named Caroline: 138,000.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.300
—Of course that's what you're doing.

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:51.620
Hey, thanks for wearing my, uh,
face on your torso, by the way.

00:00:51.620 --> 00:00:55.220
A couple other things. I signed over 200,000 copies of the US edition of Turtles All the Way Down,

00:00:55.220 --> 00:00:57.480
so hopefully you won't have trouble
finding an autographed one,

00:00:57.480 --> 00:01:00.740
unless you live outside of the US or Canada,
in which case, I'm sorry.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:04.320
Hello! Me-from-the-future here, because me-from-the-past forgot to tell you about the second thing,

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:07.140
which is that I wanted to share some of the reviews the book has gotten today.

00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:10.900
They've all been really generous. The Wall Street Journal
called it "tender, wise, and hopeful."

00:01:10.900 --> 00:01:13.820
The New York Times called it a "wrenching and revelatory novel."

00:01:13.820 --> 00:01:19.140
It got starred reviews from Booklist and SLJ, and the Guardian said it "might be a new modern classic,"

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:21.680
which is a bit much, but you know what? I'll take it.

00:01:21.680 --> 00:01:23.860
Alright, back to the past, which is in your present.

00:01:23.860 --> 00:01:26.320
Alright, we just did our first warm-up show, Hank. How did it go?

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:29.520
—Bad!
—No! It went— It went alright!

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:32.400
—Heh, okay. 
—Uh, you could kinda tell that we'd never rehearsed.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.520
—Well, this was a rehearsal,

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:38.400
and I was somewhat surprised when I found out there were gonna be 150 people there.

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:40.240
—They were very nice, though.
—Oh, very, very nice.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.740
Especially Olivia, who told me
all the words to my songs.

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:44.880
—Hank forgot the words to
every single one of his songs,

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.860
but fortunately, there was a young woman named Olivia in the front row, who had all of Hank's songs memorized,

00:01:49.860 --> 00:01:53.740
so everything worked out better than expected.
I wouldn't actually say better than expected.

00:01:53.740 --> 00:01:56.300
—[LAUGHS]
—I would say differently from expected.

00:01:56.300 --> 00:01:57.740
—It worked out just fine.

00:01:57.740 --> 00:01:59.660
Is this the final version of the book?
—It is.

00:01:59.660 --> 00:02:02.820
—What does it look like with the dust cover off?
Oh, neat, there's a secret!

00:02:02.820 --> 00:02:05.200
—There's a secret.
—[GASPS]

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.020
—There's a secret, yeah.
—I'm not gonna show you!

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:09.560
—It's pretty cool, right?
—That's great!

00:02:09.560 --> 00:02:11.820
—Yeah. That was designed by people in Nerdfighteria.

00:02:11.820 --> 00:02:14.000
—Why didn't you tell me about that?
We could've made merch from it.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:18.020
—Oh, my God. We have merch from it: it's called Turtles All the Way Down.

00:02:18.020 --> 00:02:19.400
It's available in bookstores everywhere.

00:02:19.400 --> 00:02:23.020
Okay, Hank, I'm gonna ask you some questions from our audience that we didn't get to answer during the show.

00:02:23.020 --> 00:02:28.300
If 2016 was a giant dumpster fire, what is a visual representation of 2017?

00:02:28.300 --> 00:02:31.040
—Is it just, like, what's left after a dumpster fire?

00:02:31.040 --> 00:02:33.560
—2017: the year of burnt garbage!

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:35.420
—Do you listen to music while
you're writing your books?

00:02:35.420 --> 00:02:38.680
—This will surprise you, Hank, but I do.
Only the Mountain Goats.

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:44.100
—How does it feel to have Hank be a published author?
—I'm so psyched. I'm so happy. I'm so proud of Hank.

00:02:44.100 --> 00:02:50.340
—John, If I was cast in a movie adaptation of your book, who would I play?

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.220
—I mean, that seems unlikely on a lot of levels.

00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:55.020
—Can I be the tuatara?

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:59.360
—That's actually not a bad call.
Show me your best tuatara. [SNORTS]

00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:01.020
—[NASAL VOICE] I've just got a neck cramp.

00:03:01.020 --> 00:03:06.340
—Oh, my God, that's one of the most disturbing things I've ever seen.

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:12.240
I'm gonna put up a real tuatara. Let's go back-to-back.
Is it a good impression or not? You be the judge.

00:03:12.240 --> 00:03:15.840
—But it has to have, like, some lines.
—It definitely does not have lines.

00:03:15.840 --> 00:03:19.720
The whole point of the tuatara is
that it is a cold, dead-eyed—

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:25.260
—[EXAGGERATED PSEUDO-TEXAN ACCENT] Hello, Aza! I'm the tuatara! Heyyyyyyy!

00:03:25.260 --> 00:03:27.800
—Oh, man.
—[IN ACCENT] I'm a living fossil!

00:03:27.800 --> 00:03:31.600
—Again, Turtles All the Way Down is out now,
and you can go to the subreddit.

00:03:31.600 --> 00:03:35.520
There is a link below if you wanna talk about spoilers; please don't talk about them in comments.

00:03:35.520 --> 00:03:40.580
Thank you! Thank you for reading. DFTBA. Hank, I will continue to see you right now.

